+## Whole preceding paragraph deletion — Leaf #152 follow-up (2026-11-10)
+
+Deleting a non-empty paragraph from its start through the following paragraph's
+start removes its mark as well as its text. The surviving paragraph retains its
+own paragraph properties, mark formatting and inline runs, like deleting the text
+then the resulting empty paragraph. A range retaining leading text, or entering
+part of the following text, keeps the ordinary leading-paragraph merge rule.
+Synthetic model/engine checks cover both selection directions, Delete/Backspace,
+list formatting, history, DOCX and outline membership. This is not a new native
+Word comparison or confirmation in a released Leaf build.
